SUMMARY:Panigiri of Sotiras (Transfiguration)\, Pyrgos and Kalo Ampeli
LOCATION:Pyrgos\, Serifos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Transfiguration is kept at the village of Pyrgos and at the chapel of Sotiras above Kalo Ampeli beach\, with vespers on the evening of 5 August\, the ktitores' table of fava and goat\, and liturgy on the 6th. Pyrgos is the more accessible of the two and has the village-square glenti\; Kalo Ampeli is a walk-in beach chapel and very quiet.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/serifos/#pyrgos-panigiri-of-sotiras-transfiguration-pyrgos-and-kalo-a
